  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0033","literal","Five years, scholars no false records, mourning periods not commanded yet orderly.","Five years, the shi had no conscription registers; mourning periods were orderly without being commanded.","Focus unit 士無尺籍 contrasts with the prior literal’s “scholars no false records”: 尺籍 are military conscription registers, and 士 here are men of service, not scholars. The proposed literal restores that sense; 喪期不令而治 is already rightly “mourning periods … orderly without being commanded.”","high","applied"],
    ["s0072","literal","Wen Gong said: 'Son then self consider have crime, sha ren also have crime?'","Wen Gong said: 'Son then self consider have crime, gua ren also have crime?'","Duke Wen’s speech has 寡人亦有罪邪, the ruler’s self-reference 寡人 (gua ren), not “sha ren.” Replacing the nonsensical romanization corrects a real mistranslation without changing the rest of the literal.","high","applied"],
    ["s0079","literal","Gong yizi see good cloth yet family woman expel.","Gongyi zi see good cloth yet family woman expel.","公儀子 is the honorific for Gongyi Xiu (compound surname 公儀 + 子); splitting it as “Gong yizi” is wrong. “Gongyi zi” restores the correct name segmentation while leaving the rest of the literal intact.","high","applied"]
  ],
